  "analysis": "The terminal is ready. I need to investigate the environment, specifically the location of PCAPs and the rules file. I also need to verify if Suricata is available to run tests.",
  "plan": "I will list the files in the /root directory to confirm the structure and check the current content of local.rules. I will also check the available PCAPs.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -R /root/\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/local.rules\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "suricata --build-info\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I need to inspect the contents of the positive and negative PCAP files to understand the HTTP traffic structure. This will help me verify the specific fields (method, URI, headers, body) and format the Suricata rule correctly.",
  "plan": "I will run tcpdump on both the positive and negative PCAP files to view the packet payloads in ASCII. This will allow me to see the HTTP headers and body content.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "tcpdump -n -r /root/pcaps/train_pos.pcap -A -c 20\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tcpdump -n -r /root/pcaps/train_neg.pcap -A -c 20\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I have analyzed the traffic. The positive traffic has `x-tlm-mode: exfil` and specific body patterns. The negative traffic has `x-tlm-mode: normal`. I have a plan for the Suricata rule. I need to verify the Suricata configuration to ensure `local.rules` is included, then write the rule and test it.",
  "plan": "1. Check `suricata.yaml` to confirm it includes `local.rules`. 2. Write the identified rule to `/root/local.rules`. 3. Run Suricata against both PCAPs and verify the alerts.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -A 5 \"rule-files\" /root/suricata.yaml\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep \"default-rule-path\" /root/suricata.yaml\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I have identified the necessary components for the Suricata rule based on the requirements and PCAP analysis. I need to match HTTP POST method, specific URI, specific header, and specific body patterns (Base64 blob and hex signature). I will write this rule to `local.rules` and then verify it by running Suricata against the provided PCAPs.",
  "plan": "1. Write the Suricata rule to `/root/local.rules` using a heredoc to avoid escaping issues. 2. Create output directories for logs. 3. Run Suricata manually specifying the rule file and PCAPs. 4. Check the logs to confirm the positive PCAP generates an alert and the negative one does not.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /root/local.rules <<EOF\nalert http any any -> any any (msg:\"Exfil Detected\"; flow:established,to_server; http.method; content:\"POST\"; http.uri; content:\"/telemetry/v2/report\"; pcre:\"/^\\/telemetry\\/v2\\/report$/U\"; http.header; content:\"X-TLM-Mode: exfil\"; http.request_body; content:\"blob=\"; pcre:\"/blob=[a-zA-Z0-9+\\/]{80,}/P\"; content:\"sig=\"; pcre:\"/sig=[a-fA-F0-9]{64}(?![a-fA-F0-9])/P\"; sid:1000001; rev:1;)\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /root/logs_pos /root/logs_neg\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "suricata -S /root/local.rules -r /root/pcaps/train_pos.pcap -l /root/logs_pos\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/logs_pos/fast.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "suricata -S /root/local.rules -r /root/pcaps/train_neg.pcap -l /root/logs_neg\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/logs_neg/fast.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The previous Suricata execution failed due to memory/thread allocation issues, likely because it attempted to spawn too many threads (W#108 indicates >100 threads). I need to run Suricata in single-threaded mode to avoid resource exhaustion. The rule itself appears syntactically correct, but I will verify its content before running.",
  "plan": "1. Verify the content of `local.rules`. 2. Run Suricata in single-threaded mode (`--runmode single`) against the positive PCAP. 3. Check for alerts in the positive log. 4. Run Suricata in single-threaded mode against the negative PCAP. 5. Check for alerts in the negative log (should be none).",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/local.rules\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "suricata --runmode single -S /root/local.rules -r /root/pcaps/train_pos.pcap -l /root/logs_pos\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/logs_pos/fast.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "suricata --runmode single -S /root/local.rules -r /root/pcaps/train_neg.pcap -l /root/logs_neg\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/logs_neg/fast.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The previous Suricata run produced no alerts. The most likely reason is case sensitivity in the header match. The traffic shows `x-tlm-mode: exfil`, but the rule checked for `X-TLM-Mode: exfil` without `nocase`. Suricata content matches are case-sensitive by default. I will modify the rule to include `nocase` for the header. I will also refine the PCREs to ensure they work correctly with the `http.request_body` sticky buffer, removing the `/P` flag which might be checking the wrong buffer or raw payload in a way that conflicts with the sticky buffer logic.",
  "plan": "1. Update `/root/local.rules` with the corrected rule (adding `nocase` to the header match and refining PCREs). 2. Run Suricata in single-threaded mode against the positive PCAP. 3. Verify the alert. 4. Run against the negative PCAP. 5. Verify no alerts.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /root/local.rules <<EOF\nalert http any any -> any any (msg:\"Exfil Detected\"; flow:established,to_server; http.method; content:\"POST\"; http.uri; content:\"/telemetry/v2/report\"; pcre:\"/^\\/telemetry\\/v2\\/report$/\"; http.header; content:\"X-TLM-Mode: exfil\"; nocase; http.request_body; content:\"blob=\"; pcre:\"/blob=[a-zA-Z0-9+\\/]{80,}/\"; content:\"sig=\"; pcre:\"/sig=[a-fA-F0-9]{64}(?![a-fA-F0-9])/\"; sid:1000001; rev:2;)\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "suricata --runmode single -S /root/local.rules -r /root/pcaps/train_pos.pcap -l /root/logs_pos\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/logs_pos/fast.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "suricata --runmode single -S /root/local.rules -r /root/pcaps/train_neg.pcap -l /root/logs_neg\n",
      "duration": 3.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /root/logs_neg/fast.log\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

